meta {
  name: 03 Start trial
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/centers/me/trial
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.getStatus() === 201) {
    const body = res.getBody();
    if (body.code && body.code.code) {
      bru.setEnvVar("activationKey", body.code.code);
    }
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 201
  res.body.trialEndsAt: isDefined
  res.body.code: isDefined
  res.body.code.code: isDefined
}

docs {
  Starts the 14-day free trial and issues its one activation code.

  Run `Center Auth / 03 Login` first. Fresh center must be at TRIAL_PENDING
  (`01 Get subscription`).

  ## What this does

  - Sets `trial_started_at` / `trial_ends_at` (now + 14 days).
  - Mints **one** activation code with `expiresAt` = `trialEndsAt`.
  - Captures `{{activationKey}}` for `Student Activation / 01 Activate`.

  The clock starts **here**, on the manager button — not at first student
  activation. Re-read `01 Get subscription` after: `status` TRIAL,
  `studentsMayLearn` true.

  ## Checks

  - Second call → 409 TRIAL_ALREADY_USED
  - Center that already paid → 409 ALREADY_PAID
  - No Authorization → 401

  Then: activate the student with the captured key, then
  `Subscription Access / 02 Learn`.
}
